  "comment": "mkfifo stands for make first-in-first-out . It is a command in Unix-based operating systems like Ubuntu that is used to create a *named pipe*. A pipe is an inter-process communication mechanism that allows one process to write data into the pipe while another process reads that data. Contents 1 Difference between `mkfifo` and a regular pipe: 2 Why Use `mkfifo`? 3 How to Use `mkfifo` 3.1 Creating",
